# Force LF line endings for text this repo's tooling reads byte-exact
# (generated docs compared against a fresh regeneration, unified diffs
# applied with `git apply`, JSON parsed strictly, and script source). Without
# this, a Windows checkout with the common `core.autocrlf=true` default
# silently rewrites every LF in these files to CRLF on checkout — content
# identical, bytes different — which breaks a byte-for-byte comparison
# (docs/ROUTING.md vs a fresh `routing-table.mjs` run) and a unified diff's
# own line-ending assumption (docs/proposed/*.patch) even though `git
# status`/`git diff` report nothing wrong, because the stored blob is
# untouched — only the working-tree copy is corrupted. Gate correctness
# checks on blob OIDs (`git ls-files -s`), not on git status, for exactly
# this reason.
*.md    text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf

# The pre-push hook is a POSIX sh script with no file extension. A
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true would rewrite its LFs to CRLF,
# which Git Bash's `sh` may misparse (a CRLF shebang line can fail to
# resolve the interpreter). Force LF so the committed script always runs
# the same way in Git Bash on Windows and in a real shell on Linux/macOS.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
